						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, October 13, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Visit Us! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Novus Satus is currently looking for new members. We are a active guild, seeking active yet friendly people.<BR>Please vist our site www.novussatus.com<BR><BR>Cya in Game<BR><BR>Genalebe Layurhands<BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Genalebe<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=574">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, October 04, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Do YOU have the Funk? </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							House of Funk seeking level 60+ players to experience progression instead of power gaming!  Tired of killing BoT Tower named every other day?  Want to kill Tunare, Vulak or see Vex Thal?  Then we are the place for you, check us out at http://www.hofguild.org and drop us a message on our forums.  Come join us as we progress through Luclin to Planes of Power doing content most guilds will never touch again.  New website in the works.
							<br><BR>
							 - House of Funk<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=569">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=569">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, September 30, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Chain is back! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							The guild Chain is back and is actively recruiting.
							<br><BR>
							 - Peece<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=568">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=568">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Tuesday, September 28, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">OoW Expansion Enabled? </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							When you log into game.. at Server Select Screen.. MAKE SURE YOUR OoW expansion is enabled!<BR><BR>If it is not, then make sure you check out WHY before entering game...<BR><BR>If you don't.. and have leveled PAST 65, you will be knocked down to 65.<BR><BR>Then you get to sit and wait for a GM to reimburst you after getting the expansion ENABLED!!!
							<br><BR>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=567">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, September 27, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">GAME: Escort the Gnome, Friday 10-8-04 19:00 EST </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Basic Info<BR><BR>What: Escort the Gnome Game (The Chronicles of Naughtious - 2nd Chapter)<BR>Where: Solusek Ro server, Upper Floor of Halfling Bank in Plane of Knowledge<BR>When: Participants are expected to show up between 18:00 - 19:00 EST (a Barbarian named Enormious will be waiting in the upper floor of the halfling bank in PoK, and you will need to talk to him in order to sign up for the Game) , while the Game itself will last from 19:00 - 23:00 EST.<BR>Who: Anyone who think they will survive a trip to the lair of Lord Nagafen and PvP flagged Gnomes and Halflings of lvl 6 - 13.<BR><BR><BR>Details<BR><BR>The Gnome: Naughtious, level 2 Gnomish Enchanter<BR><BR>Travel Plans: Naughtious is planning a trip to see Lord Nagafen, one of the Dragons of Norrath. This trip will take him through several zones, which are to be revealed during the Game.<BR><BR>Quests: Every zone from start to finish will involve side-quests to be finished before Naughtious will travel to the next zone. These quests will be revealed during the Game. The final Quest is to let Naughtious enter the Lair of Lord Nagafen and to be killed by the Dragon if Lord Nagafen is home.<BR><BR>Pvp Combat Quest: Once the Game begins in PoK, the participants will need to track down a Wizard named Whizby, situated somewhere in PoK. Whizby will only talk to Gnomish or Halfling PvP flagged characters, and the Game itself will be cancelled unless a minimum number of six (6) Gnomes or Halflings show up for the Game. If enough PvP players show up, Whizby will reveal the location for the first Quest of the Game - defeating an opposing PvP team (which will consist of somewhere between 1-5 lvl 9 characters).<BR><BR>Prizes: <BR>-Every PvP Gnome or Halfling which survives the PvP battle will be rewarded with 100PP.<BR>-The PvP player to deliver the final blow of the main target in the PvP battle will receieve 5.000 PP.<BR>-Every Quest in every zone throughout the Game will contain prizes to the participants which finish them first. These prizes will be revealed during the Game.<BR>-If, and only if, Naughtious completes the trip before 23:00 EST, a first prize of 10.000 PP will be rewarded to the highest roller.<BR><BR>Rules: <BR>Naughtious will not respond to any tells of any kind. Naughtious will not group with anyone. Naughtious will never run, only walk. Naughtious will not click off ANY buff placed on him. Naughtious will only attack Lord Nagafen (should the Dragon be home) and will not defend against any other creature attacking him. <BR>Naughtious does not know his way around any zones, and will wander in a pre set pattern, regardless of any attempt to give him directions. However, at a certain point, Naughtious will allow the participants to lead him towards the final goal - the Lair of Lord Nagafen. <BR>If Naughtious dies, he will accept any attempt to resurrect him, BUT.....for each time he dies, the first prize of 10.000 platinum is reduced by 1.000.<BR><BR><BR>Background:<BR>Some time ago, Naughtious travelled to see Lady Vox. This trip was successful, so now he wants to visit Lord Nagafen. However, the Dragons of Norrath do not appreciate becoming a tourist attraction for a lvl 2 Gnome, and have therefore hired a band of mercenaries to stop Naughtious from completing his trip. This means that the leader of the mercenaries must be defeated in PvP combat in order to spawn Naughtious. If this task fails, the Game ends. Any information and details around this will be revealed once the Game begins.<BR><BR>PvP Information:<BR>In order to trigger the Game to begin, at least six PvP flagged Gnomes or Halflings (minimum lvl 6 and maximum level 13) must show up for the Game. In order to become PvP flagged, you must visit the Priest of Discord, talk to him to receieve the Tome of Order and Discord and hand it back to him. This turns you into a Red Player - a PvP flagged player. Now, in order to partake in PvP combat, you have to be at least level 6. And since the opponents will be level 9, and there is a 4 level limit range on PvP combat, you cannot advance beyond level 13 in order to participate. Also, advancing beyond level 9, makes you eligible for looting. This means that if you are killed in PvP combat, you can be looted for all coin and one item (with the exception of items in bags or in Primary/Secondary/Range/Ammo slots). Advancing beyond level 9 is at own risk, but it will greatly improve the chance of defeating the mercenary group.<BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Enormious Altruisticus<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=566">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Tuesday, September 21, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Shaman epic 1.5  </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Congratulations to Foramorm <Lords of Prophecy> on completing Shaman Epic 1.5 !<BR><BR>To our knowledge he is first shaman to complete quest for Crafted Talisman of Fates on Solusek Ro.<BR><BR>Link to the item can be found here:<BR>http://www.vytco.com/images/shm_epic1_5.jpg<BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Flaor<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=565">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=565">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
